 r←DecodeUTF8 bytes;b;n;b1;b2;b3;cont;c1;c2;c3;run;lead;need;lo;hi;k;valid;start;cp;i
⍝ Decodes UTF-8 like `'UTF-8'⎕UCS`, but never fails: wherever the bytes are not valid UTF-8, the
⍝ offending sequence becomes U+FFFD, the replacement character. Follows the UTF-8 decoder of the
⍝ WHATWG Encoding Standard, which replaces each "maximal subpart" of an invalid sequence: an
⍝ overlong form, a surrogate, a code point beyond U+10FFFF, a stray continuation byte, a byte that
⍝ never occurs in UTF-8, a sequence cut short.
⍝ `'UTF-8'⎕UCS` rejects some of these with a DOMAIN ERROR, but returns others - surrogates, code
⍝ points beyond U+10FFFF - as characters that are not valid Unicode.
⍝ Works on all bytes at once. That relies on UTF-8 being self-synchronising: a byte that is not a
⍝ continuation byte (80..BF) always starts something new - a character or a U+FFFD - however the
⍝ bytes before it went. A continuation byte either belongs to the lead byte before it, or it is
⍝ a stray one and becomes a U+FFFD of its own.
⍝ A lead byte takes as many of the continuation bytes following it as it can: all it needs makes
⍝ a character, fewer make one U+FFFD - a "maximal subpart". The first continuation byte has a
⍝ narrower range after E0, ED, F0 and F4; outside it the lead byte takes none at all.
⍝ Mantis 23291 is an RFE asking for enhancing ⎕UCS so that this function can be removed.
 b←,bytes
 n←≢b
 b1←n↑1↓b                                            ⍝ The 1st, 2nd and 3rd byte after every byte;
 b2←n↑2↓b                                            ⍝ 0 beyond the end
 b3←n↑3↓b
 cont←(128≤b)∧b≤191
 c1←n↑1↓cont
 c2←n↑2↓cont
 c3←n↑3↓cont
 run←c1+(c1∧c2)+c1∧c2∧c3                             ⍝ Continuation bytes that follow, up to 3
 lead←(194≤b)∧b≤244                                  ⍝ C2..F4: C0, C1 and F5..FF never occur
 need←lead×1+(224≤b)+240≤b                           ⍝ Continuation bytes a lead byte needs
 lo←128+(32×b=224)+16×b=240                          ⍝ E0 80..9F, F0 80..8F would be overlong
 hi←191-(32×b=237)+48×b=244                          ⍝ ED A0..BF a surrogate, F4 90..BF beyond U+10FFFF
 k←((lo≤b1)∧b1≤hi)×need⌊run                          ⍝ Continuation bytes a lead byte takes
 valid←(b≤127)∨lead∧k=need
 start←~(n↑0,k≥1)∨(n↑0 0,k≥2)∨n↑0 0 0,k≥3           ⍝ Not taken by a lead byte
 cp←b
 i←⍸valid∧need=1
 cp[i]←(64×32|b[i])+64|b1[i]
 i←⍸valid∧need=2
 cp[i]←(4096×16|b[i])+(64×64|b1[i])+64|b2[i]
 i←⍸valid∧need=3
 cp[i]←(262144×8|b[i])+(4096×64|b1[i])+(64×64|b2[i])+64|b3[i]
 cp[⍸~valid]←65533
 r←⎕UCS start/cp
⍝Done
